{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1217632-mortal-weapons-with-special-powers","id":1217632,"title":"Mortal Weapons with special powers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-11T05:24:58-07:00","id":1217632,"title":"Mortal Weapons with special powers","content":"Hey there everyone<br /> <br /> Me and my GM came to talking about weapons and the sort since I am playing the crafter in our group. <br /> <br /> My character is looking into making more complex weapons such as a crossbow. The thing is we talked about if mortal weapons should have the ability to have special powers or moves? My idea was a shield that has a mechanism inside which forcefully pushes outward, thereby enhancing its smashing attack so that it dosnt get the penalty to damage from the shield tag for just that attack. This move would only be usable 4 times before it needs to the reset with a repair project. <br /> <br /> My other idea was beside the above ability that it should be able to fire a part of it out to short range and make a ranged Smash attack but doing so uses up all the above mentioned charges.<br /> <br /> What do you guys and girls think? Is these abilities too much to give to mortal weapons? Or if you have some other good ideas id love to hear them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13663-adaras","name":"Adaras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13663_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T06:05:34-07:00","id":1217641,"title":"","content":"I'm all for combining two weapons, giving an exceptional weapon having/missing a tag it doesn't normally to represent some quirk of it's construction but really not sure about upgrading existing tags.<br /> <br /> However, I'd be more flexible if this was a mortals game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 05-11-2018, 09:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T07:49:42-07:00","id":1217668,"title":"","content":"I think contraptions of this nature are fine if you're building them yourself. Power-wise there shouldn't be a problem. Arms of the Chose has the Ultimately Useful Tube, which is a 2 dot artifact staff/snorkle/blowgun/flute that is 99% usable by mortals. The only thing they can't do is spend motes to produce darts for the blowgun mode.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T09:31:18-07:00","id":1217690,"title":"","content":"Sounds cool to me, though I'd definitely say making such things should be <i>at least</i> Difficulty 5 (not that that's really much of an obstacle in practice, but still).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T09:39:39-07:00","id":1217693,"title":"","content":"Dunno if it's helpful, but what I've done in my game is allow exceptional mundane to give specialty bonuses to specific reasonable rolls.<br /> <br /> For example, our Twilight was forging a new sword for our Ice Walker Zenith. He wanted to make it fierce and imposing, so for the extra difficulty and requirements of an Exceptional item, the sword now gives a bonus die to intimidation when it's used to threaten someone","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T09:54:41-07:00","id":1217696,"title":"","content":"I would say that if a ready action were used to swift between different weapon modes most vanilla balance is kept. Like changing a crossbow into a shield. Or changing a shield into a battleaxe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T09:56:59-07:00","id":1217699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1217632-mortal-weapons-with-special-powers?p=1217693#post1217693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dunno if it's helpful, but what I've done in my game is allow exceptional mundane to give specialty bonuses to specific reasonable rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Non-weapon/armour exceptional Items providing a +1 bonus in RAW. Ex3 core page 580.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> For example, our Twilight was forging a new sword for our Ice Walker Zenith. He wanted to make it fierce and imposing, so for the extra difficulty and requirements of an Exceptional item, the sword now gives a bonus die to intimidation when it's used to threaten someone</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a cool way of giving an exceptional sword a bonus without doing bad things to the combat system.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T15:15:34-07:00","id":1217791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1217632-mortal-weapons-with-special-powers?p=1217699#post1217699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Non-weapon/armour exceptional Items providing a +1 bonus in RAW. Ex3 core page 580.<br /> <br /> This is a cool way of giving an exceptional sword a bonus without doing bad things to the combat system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I meant weapons specifically, but my brain is dodgy on the best days and phones aren't great for forum responses.<br /> <br /> Also, thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T15:25:39-07:00","id":1217796,"title":"","content":"And, thinking on it a moment longer, the same approach could in theory be used for more combat specific things. Take the above mentioned piston shield. Gives a Specialty bonus on the Smash maneuver. An extra die is always handy, doesn't come in to play if someone has Melee Specialty: Shields, but gives a nice little buff to people who aren't hyper focused like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T15:28:47-07:00","id":1217799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>light-hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1217632-mortal-weapons-with-special-powers?p=1217696#post1217696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that if a ready action were used to swift between different weapon modes most vanilla balance is kept. Like changing a crossbow into a shield. Or changing a shield into a battleaxe.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd actually be neat, kinda like Monster Hunter's various Switch weapons, or Bloodborne's everything. Noticeable nifty aid but not absurd. Switched to a crossbow? Well, those melee guys made it into sword's reach, got bad news for you...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T01:23:28-07:00","id":1218439,"title":"","content":"Hi everyone<br /> <br /> Thank you all for your insights <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> The reason for looking into this subject is that my character is very focused on making a sustainable world so she wants to create things that mortals can use without the use of essence. So she plays with around with Da Vinci esque ideas, trying to make machines and devices that can help mortals without the need for exalts. <br /> <br /> Thanks again for all your cool insights, they are really good for giving all mortals weapons a flavor without making them too strong <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13663-adaras","name":"Adaras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13663_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}